rmat="intermediate"><addressbook><name>AIZAWA, KATSUO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>AMAN, NORIAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>GOMI, SHUICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUMI, SHINJIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKAHASHI, HIROTADA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TERAYAMA, YOSHIHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Novel X-ray intercepting gold complexes of mono-L-aspartyl (or mono-L-glutamyl)chlorin e6, and salts thereof, which can cause lesions of tumors, solid cancers or arteriosclerosis to be sharply imaged by radiography and enable the therapy of the lesions by X-ray irradiation. Similar platinum complexes can be also prepared in similar manners.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne des complexes intercepteurs de rayons X à base d'or de mono-L-aspartyle(ou mono-L-glutamyle) chlore e6 et leurs sels qui peuvent provoquer des lésions de tumeurs, de cancers solides et d'artérioscléroses dont on peut obtenir des images contrastées par radiographie, ce qui permet de traiter les lésions par rayons X. On peut également préparer des complexes similaires à base de platine par procédés similaires.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreeme